   "interpretations": {
    "extraction_status": "extracted",
    "value": [
     "All of the associations with apathy were negative; as the volume in the region decreases, apathy increases. Decreased volume in the ventromedial prefrontal cortex, ventrolateral prefrontal cortex, posterior cingulate cortex and adjacent lateral cortex, and bank of the superior temporal sulcus was independently associated with apathy. These regions correspond to the Medial Prefrontal Cortex and Orbital Prefrontal Cortex networks involved in arousal, threat response, and reward processing."
